    "https://www.menlo.edu/faculty/": {
      "title": "Faculty",
      "description": "Faculty - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students GIVE APPLY BACK TO TOP Faculty At Menlo College, our faculty is a dedicated team of distinguished educators and scholars who bring real-world experience and expertise to the classroom. They are not just experts in their fields—they are mentors who are passionate about helping students succeed in their academic and career goals. Discover the faculty members who are committed to your growth and success at Menlo. Welcome, from the VP of Academic Affairs & Dean, School of Business At Menlo College, the School of Business faculty and staff are dedicated to shaping the next generation of business leaders. With deep industry experience and academic expertise, our faculty integrate Silicon Valley’s entrepreneurial spirit into the classroom, ensuring students are prepared for the evolving demands of global markets. Our faculty not only teach but also serve as mentors, providing students with the tools and insights to excel in today’s dynamic business landscape. Whether you are pursuing an undergraduate degree or advancing your career through our graduate programs—the Master of Science in Information Systems (MSIS) or Master of Science in Financial Technology (MSFT)—you will benefit from personalized attention and a curriculum designed to bridge theory with real-world application. Through our unique Global Immersion Program and Silicon Valley Immersion experiences, students gain invaluable exposure to cutting-edge industries and global business practices. Explore our directory and connect with the accomplished faculty and staff in the School of Business who will guide you through your academic and professional journey at Menlo College. —Dr. Mouwafac Sidaoui, VP of Academic Affairs & Dean, School of Business School of Business Faculty & Staff Directory Welcome, from the Dean of Arts & Sciences At Menlo College, Arts & Sciences courses are the foundation of every degree, equipping students with essential skills in communication, critical thinking, and quantitative reasoning. Our dedicated faculty are committed to expanding your horizons, fostering intellectual curiosity, and preparing you for success in an ever-evolving world. Whether you’re engaging with general education courses, pursuing a major in Psychology, or complementing your studies with one of our interdisciplinary minors, our faculty are here to support and challenge you. For those interested in graduate studies, Menlo also offers a Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology (MASPP), providing a direct pathway to careers in counseling, coaching, and sports performance. Explore our directory to learn more about the passionate educators who will guide you on your academic journey. —Dr. Melissa R. Michelson, Dean of Arts & Sciences Arts & Sciences Faculty Directory Learn More About Menlo Ready to explore Menlo College? Take the first step towards a rewarding academic journey. Fill out the form below to receive more information about our programs, campus life, financial aid options, and admissions process. We’re excited to connect with you and help you discover your future. First Name Last Name Email Phone Number I agree to receive text messages from Menlo College, including updates, reminders, and event information Please select... Yes No Message and data rates may apply I would like to receive telephone calls that deliver AI messages and SMS that provide details about Menlo College at this telephone number Please select... I consent to be contacted by Menlo College via AI-powered telephone calls and SMS at the mobile phone number provided. I do not consent to be contacted by Menlo College via AI-powered telephone calls or SMS at the mobile phone number provided. Message and data rates may apply Your Journey Begins Here Apply Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
