    "https://www.menlo.edu/career-connect-day/": {
      "title": "Career Connect Day",
      "description": "Career Connect Day - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students GIVE APPLY BACK TO TOP Career Connect Day Check out past events Save the Date for Career Connect Day: March 3, 2027 Every spring, Menlo College’s Career Connect Day brings together students, alumni, and industry professionals for a day of networking and career exploration. With no classes held that day, students can focus entirely on their career development. Students will hear from industry experts on topics like navigating the job search and leveraging AI, followed by a Career Fair connecting them with employers offering internships, part-time, and full-time opportunities. Career Connect Day is the perfect chance to gain new skills, make connections, and advance your career journey. More Information and Speaker Lineup Coming Soon \"Career Connect Day is our gateway to endless possibilities, where your passion meets the opportunity to build a future.\" Elijah Valdeolivar Senior Associate Director of Employer Relations & Career Services Thank you to our sponsors Presenting Sponsor: Gold Sponsor: Silver Sponsor: Silver Sponsor: Career Connect Day Archive Career Connect Day 2026 Speaker Lineup Career Connect Day 2025 Your Journey Begins Here Apply Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
