      "title": "Adjunct Instructors: Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructors: Psychology - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Adjunct Instructors: Psychology Adjunct Instructors: Psychology Menlo College is seeking adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate courses in Psychology. To be considered for a teaching position, a candidate must have a master’s degree and previous college teaching experience in this subject matter. Applications will be screened by the Office of Academic Affairs and qualified applicants who best meet the needs of the College will be contacted for an interview. About Menlo College Menlo College is a diverse and tight-knit community of exceptional, involved people. Our mission is to: “…ignite potential and educate students to make meaningful contributions in the innovation economy.” We attract students from all over the world who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and making an impact in their communities. Continuing an unbroken streak for more than a decade, Menlo College was named to the most recent Princeton Review “Best Colleges” list, recognition given to only 12% of all colleges and universities in the U.S. Menlo College was also ranked #11 in Money for Best Business Colleges in the U.S. Menlo College is designated as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and an Asian American and Native American, Pacific Islander-Serving Institution (AANAPISI). Only 1% of all colleges and universities in the U.S. achieve this dual recognition. Our campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco, in Silicon Valley – one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with exceptional opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College’s School of Business offers bachelor’s degree programs, ten majors, and two graduate degree programs. Menlo College is accredited by AACSB and WSCUC. Application Process Contact Human Resources 1000 El Camino Real Atherton, CA 94027-4301 650.543.3733 phone hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/intensive-english-program-tesol-ell-instruction/": {
      "title": "Intensive English Program / TESOL / ELL Instruction",
      "description": "Intensive English Program / TESOL / ELL Instruction - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Intensive English Program / TESOL / ELL Instruction Intensive English Program / TESOL / ELL Instruction Menlo College is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach English language learners within its Intensive English Program. To be considered for a teaching position, a candidate must meet the following qualifications: Have at least a master’s degree from an accredited institution of higher learning in English or TESOL or a related discipline Demonstrate previous college-level experience working with English language learners and have knowledge of the concepts and practices of TESOL Be committed to providing excellence in education and fostering a dynamic and welcoming learning environment Have the ability to work closely with a diverse student body and the IEP team of instructors About Menlo College Menlo College is a diverse and tight-knit community of exceptional, involved people. Our mission is to: “…ignite potential and educate students to make meaningful contributions in the innovation economy.” We attract students from all over the world who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and making an impact in their communities. Continuing an unbroken streak for more than a decade, Menlo College was named to the most recent Princeton Review “Best Colleges” list, recognition given to only 12% of all colleges and universities in the U.S. Menlo College was also ranked #11 in Money for Best Business Colleges in the U.S. Menlo College is designated as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and an Asian American and Native American, Pacific Islander-Serving Institution (AANAPISI). Only 1% of all colleges and universities in the U.S. achieve this dual recognition. Our campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco, in Silicon Valley – one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with exceptional opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College’s School of Business offers bachelor’s degree programs, ten majors, and two graduate degree programs. Menlo College is accredited by AACSB and WSCUC. Application Process Applications will be screened by the Office of Academic Affairs, and qualified applicants who best meet the needs of the College will be contacted for an interview. Please submit materials to: Menlo College Human Resources 1000 El Camino Real Atherton, CA 94027-4301 or via email to: hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/sports-management-visiting-professor/": {
      "title": "Sports Management Visiting Professor- Full-Time, One Semester (Spring 2027)",
      "description": "Sports Management Visiting Professor- Full-Time, One Semester (Spring 2027) - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Sports Management Visiting Professor- Full-Time, One Semester (Spring 2027) Sports Management Visiting Professor- Full-Time, One Semester (Spring 2027) Reports to: Dean, School of Business Compensation: $85,000-$110,000 per annum, commensurate with experience ($42,500 – $55,000 for the semester) Application Deadline: Preference given to applications received by Nov. 15, 2026 Target Start Date: January 2027 Position Overview Menlo College seeks a qualified instructor to offer undergraduate courses in Sports Management. Courses may include introduction to sports management, research methods in sports management, sports analytics, marketing & advertising in the sports industry, sports sponsorship & sales management, ethics in sports management, history of sports, and the economics of sports, among other topics. We are particularly interested in a candidate with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and who will contribute to diversity and equal opportunity in higher education through their teaching or other related areas. Qualifications The successful candidate should have an earned doctorate or MS in Sports Management or in a related field from a reputable university in hand prior to the start of the Spring 2027 semester (January 2027). Preference will be given to candidates with a strong record of effective undergraduate teaching as the instructor of record. Candidates must be able and qualified to teach undergraduate sports management classes. They must also possess strong interpersonal skills and be able to work in a collaborative and collegial environment. Responsibilities The position requires undergraduate teaching in sports management, mentoring and advising undergraduate students, and active ongoing engagement in shared governance and other service assignments at the collegiate level, including assessment of learning. The usual faculty load is 12 units (usually four three-unit classes) each semester. About Menlo College Menlo College is doing transformative work with an significantly diverse population of students, about one-third of whom are the first in their families to attend college. Almost 100 years old, this small gem of a private college – with fewer than 900 students – is changing lives and providing a stream of inspiring, diverse and capable graduates to Silicon Valley companies and organizations. The private school offers four-year undergraduate degrees in business and psychology, and three graduate programs that leverage key areas of excellence within the College. Menlo College faculty members teach and mentor from their perspectives as scholars, entrepreneurs, managers, and community leaders. Menlo College attracts students from all over the world — young adults who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and volunteering in the community. The campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco in Silicon Valley, one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with many opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College is consistently featured in lists of America’s best colleges, including citations by the Princeton Review. AffordableCollegesOnline.org (AC Online) has brought additional recognition to the quality of the Menlo College experience when the organization named Menlo as one of the 4-year colleges in California with the best lifetime return on investment (ROI). The diversity of Menlo students is reflected in two federal designations: as a Hispanic-Serving Institution and as an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution. Menlo is also one of the safest campuses anywhere; Universities.com ranks Menlo first in California, and fourth in the nation as the “safest college campus in America.” Application Process Submitted applications should include a letter of interest that discusses teaching philosophy and research interests, a current CV, names and contact information for 3 references, and teaching evaluations (if available). Please submit materials by November 15, 2026. Please email material to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a criminal background check. Menlo College is committed to a firm policy of equal employment opportunity. Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/student-career-services/": {
      "title": "Student Services",
      "description": "Student Services - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students GIVE APPLY BACK TO TOP Career Services > Student Services Student Services The Office of Internships & Career Services (ICS) is here to help guide students on their paths to meaningful careers. We do this through individual advising, workshops and events, Career Connect Day and the Internship Program. Career Connect Day Internship Program Internship Program Completing at least one internship is a graduation requirement for all business majors, and optional as an elective for psychology majors. Our Academic Internship Program offers students invaluable hands-on experience, helping them build their professional network and apply classroom learning to real-world situations. Learn more about our flagship Menlo College Internship Program! Explore Internship Program On-Campus Jobs & Federal Work Study Menlo College Career Services assists students in finding on-campus job opportunities and helps eligible students apply their Federal Work Study award towards on-campus employment. These experiences allow students to gain practical skills while earning income to support their education. For personalized information on eligibility, contact the Office of Financial Aid at: financialaid@menlo.edu . International Student Work Authorization For international students studying in the U.S. on an F-1 visa, we work with International Student Services (ISS) to facilitate work authorization requests for Curricular Practical Training (CPT) . International students on an F-1 visa can only work in the U.S. with authorization from a Designated School Official (DSO) in International Student Services (ISS) . For information on starting the internship process, please contact our office at careerservices@menlo.edu . For information on Curricular Practical Training (CPT), Optional Practical Training (OPT), and working in the U.S. as an international student, please contact iss@menlo.edu . We’re here to ensure you meet all the requirements and take advantage of work opportunities available to international students. Email Career Services Additional Resources Handshake is the #1 way college students find jobs. Join our Menlo College platform today and you’ll have access to the following: Search for and apply to internships and jobs, including open on-campus positions . Schedule 1:1 appointments with an ICS team member Access and download valuable resources View a calendar of career-related events Connect with employers on the platform All students can log in using their single sign-on credentials. Need more help? Watch this 5-minute tutorial on how to log in and use Handshake. Image Source: learning.linkedin.com LinkedInLearning.com is an online education company offering thousands of video courses in software, creative, and business skills. Menlo College has teamed up with LinkedInLearning to offer students free and unlimited access. Email careerservices@menlo.edu for more information. The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Menlo College to help you excel in your job search. The Academy focuses on mastering the 5 key areas of the job search so you feel confident every step of the way–because everyone deserves better work. Learn More about Job Search Academy Menlo College Career Guide Check out the below resources for support and best practices on invaluable career-building skills: Resume Toolkit Cover Letter Toolkit Dress for Success Guide Career Assessments List (schedule a meeting with a career advisor to learn more about these assessments, and for help interpreting your results!) Planning for Graduate School Visit our graduate school resources page to learn how to research, prepare for, and apply to graduate school. Whether you want to pursue a master’s or doctorate, we strongly encourage you to discuss your plans with an ICS staff member. Learn more about Menlo College’s current graduate programs here . Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Resources Click here to access an extensive and growing list of resources relevant to specific affinity groups and diverse populations. Menlo College is committed to supporting students from historically underrepresented backgrounds. Explore the links below to gain key insights on resources dedicated to supporting DE&I. Menlo College DEI Resource List An extensive list of resources relevant to specific affinity groups and diverse populations. DiversityJobs.com Where candidates can search for jobs from diversity-friendly employers, upload resumes, opt for free job alerts delivered via email Gorick Diversity Pipeline Programs List of organizations dedicated to hiring students from underrepresented backgrounds Education Cost Resources Tips on how to earn additional income to offset the cost of college Contact Career Services Contact Internships and Career Services (ICS) Schedule an Appointment careerservices@menlo.edu Your Journey Begins Here Apply Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    }
  },
